cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  FBSI is published in Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering
  461 (2026) 119161 (https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cma.2026.119161). If you use
  the method or this software, please cite this paper (see preferred-citation).
type: software
title: "FBSI: Face-Based Soft-Intersection particle-to-cell volume mapping"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation (Python and C++) of the Face-Based Soft-Intersection
  (FBSI) method for computing the fraction of each particle's volume inside each
  computational cell in Lagrangian-Eulerian (CFD-DEM) simulations. Each cell is
  represented as the intersection of soft half-spaces defined by its face normals,
  giving an anisotropic, tuning-free, volume-conserving and smooth mapping on
  structured and unstructured meshes.
